---
import SignalMast from "../components/SignalMast.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy — Satyajit Roy" description="How the portfolio handles the small amount of data it needs.">
  <div class="frame field-layout">
    <SignalMast enabledSources={["curated"]} />
    <article class="content-field privacy-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Small data surface. Explicit boundaries.</h1>
      <p class="intro">This portfolio is static-first. It does not run behavioural analytics, tracking pixels, third-party font requests, or social media embeds.</p>

      <section>
        <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>The newsletter is not accepting subscriptions. This site does not collect or retain email addresses until a sender domain and self-hosted double-opt-in delivery boundary are configured.</p>
      <p>Featured playlists are static cards with direct Spotify links. The browser makes no Spotify request until you choose to open one; this site does not receive listening data or embed Spotify media.</p>
      <p>The Aero India carousel serves owner-approved image files from this site. Selecting a photo opens the public Google Photos album; Google’s privacy terms apply only after that deliberate navigation.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Selected public sources</h2>
        <p>When enabled, provider cards are server-collected and cached. The browser does not receive provider credentials or contact vendor APIs directly. Each public card identifies its source and refresh time.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Infrastructure</h2>
        <p>Private infrastructure state, addresses, service inventory, logs, and topology are not published through this site. A homelab story may contain deliberately coarse, owner-approved aggregate information.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>For a data request, use the owner-approved contact route when it is published. A future newsletter will provide a one-click unsubscribe path in every confirmed email.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-page { max-width: 52rem; padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 6rem); }
  h1, h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.06em; }
  h1 { margin: 0.5rem 0 1.3rem; font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.7rem); line-height: 0.84; }
  .intro { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.2rem; }
  h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.1rem); }
  section p { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
